# ---- runtime state written by the backoffice ----
# Uploads (Bottle Asset Configurator) and, since the client owns her own
# password, data/admin/credentials.json. None of it is source, and the
# credentials file must never be in a repository. On the server this whole
# directory has to be a persistent volume — otherwise a deploy wipes the
# client's password and the handover credential silently takes over again.
data/

# isolated verification builds
.next-verify/
.next-verify*/
.next*/
*.pack

.vercel

# ---- credentials ----
# `.env*` only catches files that START with a dot. prod.env walked straight
# past it and sat in the repository with ADMIN_PASSWORD and a VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN
# inside (commit 9830e43, taken back out 2026-09-03). The second pattern
# catches every spelling: .env, .env.local, prod.env, staging.env — and so
# replaces the explicit `prod.env` line from 63dd59f, which it already covers.
# prod.env.example is not matched — it documents the names, never the values.
.env*
*.env
